gpui_windows: Owned file drops

A window opened with `WindowOptions::local_file_drop` registers
DragAcceptFiles instead of an OLE drop target. On WM_DROPFILES it copies
the dropped paths, the final position and the client geometry, without
calling the source's COM objects or the file system, and hands them to
the `on_native_file_drop` callback after native dispatch. Admission must
be enabled explicitly, and a move, resize, DPI or activation change
invalidates a drop still queued.

Newport needs it for Remote apps on Windows: files dropped from Explorer
go to the Linux app under the cursor.

This is a second drop path beside GPUI's OLE drop target, and such a
window gets no FileDropEvent. on_native_file_drop and
set_native_file_drop_enabled have defaults. WindowOptions gains a
Windows-only local_file_drop field, so struct literals on Windows must
set it or use `..Default::default()`.

Remove when upstream gpui_windows can deliver file drops with their final
position and paths outside native dispatch.

